  "body": "## Issue\nCloses #763\nCloses #793\nRefs #768 (the `<svg>`/`<math>` follow-up of the round-5 review of #771; #768's part 2, the `R267a` prose handle, stays open)\nClaim: cloud/i763-opus\n\n## What and why\n**Problem.** A member's signature (and mood) is member input. With `… </span>TEXT<span class=\"x\">…` inside it, `anonymize` stopped at the stray `</span>`, so `TEXT` survived, and `check` reported nothing (it only looked inside the span).\n\n**Cause.** The block's end came from a depth count of `<span>` tags, which the member's own markup can unbalance (a stray `</span>`, `</div>`, `</td>` ends it early, an unclosed `<span>` makes it run on into the next message). `check` had no rule on what follows a signature or mood.\n\n**Change.**\n- `anonymize` (`PERSONAL_BOUNDARIES`, `_personal_blocks`, `_personal_block_end`): a signature or mood runs to the last `</span>` before the next element HFR prints after it, which a member cannot write. From the whole corpus (2026-11-11): every signature is followed by `</span></div></td></tr></table>` then the next `table.messagetable`, the footer's `tr.cBackHeader…` or `<br /><script>`; every mood (470 of 470) by `div.avatar_center`, `span.TransactionsReportsLink` or `td.messCase2`. Every opening is redacted, even when a depth count ran past it. With no boundary in the page, the depth count stays.\n- `check` (`StructuralVerifier`, own list `_V_AFTER_END`, LESSONS 33-34): between a signature or mood and that next element, only end tags, blanks, a bare `<br>` and the footer's numbers-only `<table>`; a signature or mood span carries only `class`, with exactly its own token; any `<svg>` or `<math>` is unexpected markup (html.parser reads `<style>`/`<script>` as raw text where a browser does not, #768); any `<[CDATA[` outside an XML document too (html.parser swallows it to `]]>`, a browser ends it at the first `>`; the AQ feed `T01` is XML and keeps its CDATA).\n- Issue point 2 (`title=`, empty `<a href>`, ``'&lt;img alt/src&gt;'``) was already refused by #771's walk; the new test pins it next to the class rule.\n- README: the new rules.\n- Round-2 Low findings (forged boundary, no boundary, silent cut, three test gaps): follow-up #797.\n\n## How it was verified\nTests first, each round red before its change (`python3 -m unittest tests.test_anonymize`):\n- Round 0, 6 failures: stray `</span>` in a signature; stray `</span>` + `</div>`; content after a signature; extra class token; `<svg>`/`<math>`; mood.\n- Round 1 (after the review), 6 failures: `test_unbalanced_ends_in_a_signature_are_redacted_too` (stray `</div></td>`, `</table>`, with footer or script after), `test_unbalanced_start_in_a_signature_stops_at_the_next_message` (unclosed `<span>`/`<div>`/`<td>` no longer swallows message 2, whose signature is redacted too), `test_unbalanced_span_end_in_a_mood_does_not_end_the_redaction` (avatar, transactions link, or nothing after), `test_check_refuses_content_after_a_signature` / `…_after_a_mood` (assert the reason, with a redacted mood), `test_check_refuses_svg_math_and_cdata`.\n- Mutation: removing each new rule makes at least one test fail (after-state arming, text rule, svg/math, CDATA, boundary end, `re.I` on `</SPAN >`).\n\nAfter the change:\n- `python3 -m unittest discover tooling/fixtures/tests`: OK.\n- `python3 tooling/fixtures/anonymize.py check --corpus Packages/HFRKit/Tests/HFRParsingTests/Fixtures/captures --quiet`: `ok 691 of 691 corpus files clean`.\n- `python3 tooling/fixtures/manifest_check.py`: OK.\n- Old vs new `anonymize` on every HTML page of the corpus (282), public and private mode: identical output, so no over-redaction.\n\nLinux-only change (`tooling/fixtures/` only): the macOS jobs are skipped (checked on 90a96d8 and 7c1e5a4).\n\n## Checklist (AGENTS.md §9)\n- [x] Module boundaries respected (tooling only)\n- [x] Tests added, seen red first\n- [x] No secrets; invented names only\n- [x] Docs: `tooling/fixtures/README.md`\n- [x] Author model: Opus / Reviewer model: Fable (round 1 REQUEST CHANGES, round 2 APPROVE on 7c1e5a4; both verdicts posted on this PR)\n- [x] No legacy behaviour or gap row: no ledger\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CETDfMpvh9JwfngVyq",
