   "body": "**Adversarial review round 1 (Fable, read-only sub-agent), verbatim:**\n\nREQUEST CHANGES\n\n**Adversarial review (claude-fable-5-2): REQUEST CHANGES** — head 90a96d8\n\nAll paths are under `/home/user/HFRnow/`. `message()` below is the tests' helper.\n\n1. **High** — `tooling/fixtures/anonymize.py:757-774` and `:2294`. Member text still survives `anonymize` and `check` reports 0. Input: `message('Jean Exemple</span></div>Secret Handle</td>Other Words<div style=\"clear: both;\"> </div>')`. The stray `</div>` and `</td>` end both depth-counted containers early; output keeps `…Signature removed.</span></div>Secret Handle</td>Other Words…`. `after_signature` is set only on the direct parent, so text after the parent's end tag is unchecked. Fix: bound the signature by HFR markup the member cannot emit (next message table or end of messages), and keep the check armed until `td.messCase2` or the row closes.\n2. **Medium** — `anonymize.py:759`. Mood is left to the depth count: `mood='<span class=\"MoodStatus\">Kilo</span>Secret Handle<span class=\"x\">Lima</span>'` keeps `Secret Handle` and `Lima`, `check` reports 0. Same class as fact 1. Fix: bound by the cell's known HFR tail, and a check rule on `td.messCase1`.\n3. **Medium** — `tooling/fixtures/tests/test_anonymize.py:701-711`. `test_check_refuses_content_after_a_signature_in_its_container` stays green with both `after_signature` rules disabled: the default mood `Kilo Lima` is what trips the check. With `mood=''`, all three inputs give 0 findings without the rules. Fix: pass a redacted mood and assert the reason.\n4. **Low** — `anonymize.py:765-774`. An unbalanced `<div>` or `<td>` in a signature makes the container run on: in a two-message page the whole second message disappears, and `check` reports 0. Add a test and stop at the next message.\n5. **Low** — `tooling/fixtures/README.md:71,136` do not describe the new rules (nothing after a signature, class-only span, svg/math).\n6. **Low** (same class as #768, already in base) — `anonymize.py:2233`. `<td class=\"messCase1\"><[CDATA[ <b class=\"s2\">Real Handle</b> ]]></td>` gives 0 findings: `html.parser` swallows it to `]]>`, a browser ends the bogus comment at the first `>`. Fix: flag `unknown_decl` everywhere.\n7. **Detail** — no test fails when the `PARA_OPEN_RE` container, `len(attrs) != 1`, `re.I` on `SPAN_END_RE`, or the `> end` guard is removed.\n\n**Verified**: unit tests 379 OK; `check --corpus` 691/691 clean; `manifest_check.py` OK. Head and base give identical output on 1384 corpus runs (public and private), so no over-redaction on real pages. Findings 1, 2, 4 and 6 probed on scratch copies of head and base; 3 and 7 by mutation.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
