   "body": "**Adversarial review round 2 (Fable, read-only sub-agent), verbatim:**\n\nAPPROVE\n\n**Adversarial review (claude-fable-5-2): APPROVE** — head 7c1e5a4\n\nRound-1 findings 1 to 6 are fixed, and all round-1 inputs are now redacted with `check` clean. Remaining findings are Low and non-blocking; a follow-up issue would cover them. All paths are under `/home/user/HFRnow/`; `message()` and `PAGES` are the tests' helpers.\n\n1. **Low** — `tooling/fixtures/anonymize.py:758-763` and `:2118-2122`. A forged boundary inside the member's markup leaks through both sides. `message('Jean Exemple</span><table class=\"messagetable\"><tr><td>Secret Handle</td></tr></table><span>') + PAGES` keeps `Secret Handle`, `check` reports 0. Same with `</span><script>Secret Handle</script><span>`, and in a mood with `<div class=\"avatar_center\">` or `<td class=\"messCase2\">`. This needs a member able to write attribute-bearing HFR tags, beyond the issue's unbalanced-tag model. Fix: for a signature, refuse a boundary seen while its `td.messCase2` is still open.\n2. **Low** — `anonymize.py:783-785` and `:2260-2276`. With no boundary after the signature, the redactor falls back to the depth count and the verifier ignores comments, declarations, processing instructions and end-tag attributes after the span. `message('Jean Exemple</span><!-- Secret Handle -->')` without `PAGES` keeps the comment, `check` reports 0; same for `</span></b title=\"Secret Handle\">`. No corpus page has this shape. Fix: raise when no boundary follows, and flag those non-elements while `after_personal` is set.\n3. **Low** — `anonymize.py:786-789`. An HFR `</span>` between the block and its boundary that is not in the list is deleted silently, `check` 0. Invented example: `<br/><span class=\"MDStatus\">…</span>` after a mood with no avatar. No corpus page is affected. Fix: raise unless the text between the chosen `</span>` and the boundary is only end tags, blanks and `<br>`.\n4. **Detail** — no test fails when the XML exemption (`:3241`), the footer-table attribute restriction (`:2125-2127`) or the bare-`br` condition is removed.\n\n**Verified**: unit tests 383 OK; `check --corpus` 691/691 clean; `manifest_check.py` OK. Head and base give identical output on 1384 corpus runs (public and private), so no over-redaction on real pages. All 336 corpus signatures are followed by a listed boundary. Mutation: each after-signature, after-mood, boundary and CDATA rule now fails a test when removed.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
